        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Beverley Knight, Sam Cooke, Aretha Franklin\n- Products: The B-Funk, Flavour of the Old School\n- Roles: recording artist, radio presenter, musical theatre actress, singer, songwriter, entrepreneur\n- Concepts: American soul music, British R&B\n\nFacts:\n- Sam Cooke, born Samuel Dale Cook, lived from January 22, 1931 to December 11, 1964 and was an American singer, songwriter, and entrepreneur.\n- Beverley Knight was born Beverley Anne Smith on 22 March 1973 and is an English recording artist, radio presenter, and musical theatre actress.\n- Beverley Knight was heavily influenced by American soul music icons including Sam Cooke and Aretha Franklin.\n- Beverley Knight released her debut album, The B-Funk, in 1995.\n- Flavour of the Old School is a song by British R&B artist Beverley Knight and was released as her debut single from her debut album The B-Funk in 1995.\n- Beverley Knight has released eight studio albums to date.",
